UnitPoolVault::constructor
├── When access router is invalid
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_InvalidAccessRouter
└── When called
    └── It should set the access router

UnitPoolVault::Initialize
├── When called on implementation
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
├── Given already initialized
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
└── Given not initialized
    ├── It should initialize UUPSUpgradeable
    ├── It should initialize Pausable
    ├── It should initialize ReentrancyGuard
    ├── It should initialize RootBuffer with ROOT_HISTORY_SIZE
    ├── It should initialize TransactVerifierRouter with verifier configs
    ├── It should configure verifiers
    ├── It should set the ASP registry
    ├── It should set the keystore
    ├── It should set the ragequit verifier
    ├── It should set the deposit verifier
    ├── It should set the max state tree size
    └── It should not be paused

UnitPoolVault::Deposit
├── When contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── When caller does not have the DEPOSITOR_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has the DEPOSITOR_ROLE
    ├── When proof is not valid
    │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidDepositProof
    ├── When proof context does not match note data
    │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_ProofContextMismatch
    └── Given proof is valid
        ├── When commitment was already used
        │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_CommitmentAlreadyUsed
        ├── Given state tree is at capacity
        │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_StateTreeFull
        ├── Given asset is native
        │   ├── When msg_value does not equal proof_value
        │   │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidValue
        │   └── When msg_value equals proof_value
        │       ├── It should record the commitment creation timestamp
        │       ├── It should insert the output commitment + timestamp into the state tree
        │       ├── It should update the commitment tree root
        │       ├── It should emit a LeavesInserted event
        │       ├── It should emit a Note event
        │       └── It should emit a Deposited event
        └── Given asset is not native
            ├── When msg_value is not zero
            │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_UnexpectedETHAmount
            ├── When transferring proof_value assets to the pool fails by returning false
            │   └── It should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation
            ├── When transferring proof_value assets to the pool fails by reverting
            │   └── It should bubble up revert data
            └── When transferring proof_value assets to the pool succeeds
                ├── It should record the commitment creation timestamp
                ├── It should insert the output commitment + timestamp into the state tree
                ├── It should update the commitment tree root
                ├── It should emit a LeavesInserted event
                ├── It should emit a Deposited event
                └── It should emit a Note event

UnitPoolVault::Transact
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── When caller is not processor
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidProcessor
├── When proof context does not match
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_ProofContextMismatch
├── Given commitment state tree root is unknown
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_UnknownStateRoot
├── Given keystore root is unknown
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_UnknownKeystoreRoot
├── Given ASP root does not match latest
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidASPRoot
├── When transact proof verification fails
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidTransactProof
├── Given commitment already used
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_CommitmentAlreadyUsed
├── Given nullifier already spent
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_NullifierAlreadySpent
├── Given state tree batch would exceed capacity
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_StateTreeFull
├── When withdrawnValue is zero
│   ├── When tokenIdOut is not zero
│   │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_TokenIdMustBeZeroOnInternalTransfer
│   ├── It should append output commitments to commitments mapping
│   ├── It should insert timestamped output commitments into state tree
│   ├── It should insert timestamped nullifiers into state tree
│   ├── It should update root buffer
│   ├── It should mark all nullifiers as spent at block.timestamp
│   ├── It should not transfer any tokens
│   ├── It should call verifyProof with correct params
│   ├── It should emit a Note event per output
│   ├── It should emit a LeavesInserted event
│   └── It should emit Transacted event
└── When withdrawnValue is not zero
    ├── When asset is native
    │   ├── When transfer fails
    │   │   └── It should revert with SafeTransferLib.ETHTransferFailed
    │   └── When transfer succeeds
    │       ├── It should append output commitments to commitments mapping
    │       ├── It should insert timestamped output commitments into state tree
    │       ├── It should insert timestamped nullifiers into state tree
    │       ├── It should update root buffer
    │       ├── It should mark all nullifiers as spent at block.timestamp
    │       ├── It should transfer ETH to caller
    │       ├── It should emit a Note event per output
    │       ├── It should emit a LeavesInserted event
    │       └── It should emit Transacted event
    └── When transact asset is ERC20
        ├── It should append output commitments to commitments mapping
        ├── It should insert timestamped output commitments into state tree
        ├── It should insert timestamped nullifiers into state tree
        ├── It should update root buffer
        ├── It should mark all nullifiers as spent at block.timestamp
        ├── It should transfer ERC20 to caller
        ├── It should emit a Note event per output
        ├── It should emit a LeavesInserted event
        └── It should emit Transacted event

UnitPoolVault::Ragequit
├── When caller does not match owner address from proof
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidOwnerAddress
├── When proof value is zero
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_ZeroValueRagequit
├── Given commitment does not exist in state tree
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_CommitmentNotFound
├── Given nullifier already spent
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_NullifierAlreadySpent
├── Given keystore root is unknown
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_UnknownKeystoreRoot
├── When ragequit proof verification fails
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidRagequitProof
├── Given state tree is at capacity
│   └── It should revert with PoolVault_StateTreeFull
└── When all checks pass
    ├── When asset is native
    │   ├── When ETH transfer fails
    │   │   └── It should revert with SafeTransferLib.ETHTransferFailed
    │   └── When ETH transfer succeeds
    │       ├── It should be callable regardless of pause state
    │       ├── It should mark nullifier as spent
    │       ├── It should insert timestamped nullifier into state tree
    │       ├── It should update root buffer
    │       ├── It should transfer ETH to caller
    │       └── It should emit Ragequit event
    └── When ragequit asset is ERC20
        ├── When transferring assets fails by returning false
        │   └── It should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation
        ├── When transferring assets fails by reverting
        │   └── It should bubble up revert data
        └── When transferring assets succeeds
            ├── It should be callable regardless of pause state
            ├── It should mark nullifier as spent
            ├── It should insert timestamped nullifier into state tree
            ├── It should update root buffer
            ├── It should transfer ERC20 to caller
            └── It should emit Ragequit event

UnitPoolVault::Pause
├── Given caller does not have PAUSER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has PAUSER_ROLE
    ├── It should pause the contract
    └── It should emit Paused event

UnitPoolVault::Unpause
├── Given caller does not have UNPAUSER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UNPAUSER_ROLE
    ├── It should unpause the contract
    └── It should emit Unpaused event

UnitPoolVault::UpgradeToAndCall
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    └── It should upgrade successfully

UnitPoolVault::SetMaxStateTreeSize
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── When new max size is less than or equal to current tree size
    │   └── It should revert with PoolVault_InvalidMaxTreeSize
    └── When new max size is greater than current tree size
        ├── It should set the max state tree size
        └── It should emit MaxStateTreeSizeUpdated event

UnitPoolVault::SetAspRegistry
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── It should set the ASP registry
    └── It should emit AspRegistrySet event

UnitPoolVault::SetKeystore
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── It should set the keystore
    └── It should emit KeystoreSet event

UnitPoolVault::SetRagequitVerifier
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── It should set the ragequit verifier
    └── It should emit RagequitVerifierSet event

UnitPoolVault::SetDepositVerifier
├── Given caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── Given caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    ├── It should set the deposit verifier
    └── It should emit DepositVerifierSet event

